    <h1 style="margin-top:14px">If you registered, you had <em>already used an automation</em></h1>
    <p class="dek">One way I've found to start citizen development<span class="gloss" data-aud="gen"> (staff outside IT building their own apps and automations with no-code tools)</span>: make the sign-up the first automation people use, and organize support around what they are trying to do. Shown through an invented library system.</p>
    <p class="tldr" data-aud="gen"><b>In short</b>Citizen development means people outside IT building their own tools. One approach that has worked for me: make the sign-up form for the first session an automation, then show people how it worked, so they can build their own.</p>
