<!-- THE SYSTEM -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="system" aria-labelledby="h-sys">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">The system</p>
    <h2 id="h-sys">A citizen development program, not a course</h2>
    <p>The program runs as a loop, and each channel in it has one job.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-sys-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">The loop</p>
        <h3>Activate, learn, build, support, listen, adapt</h3>
        <p>The program is built to cycle: what people say in one round shapes the next one.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-sys-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Start small</p>
        <h3>A first goal you can reach</h3>
        <p>The first round is a cohort small enough to support one person at a time. A small first target keeps early success within reach.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-sys-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">One job per channel</p>
        <h3>Guidance, community and people</h3>
        <p>Intranet pages hold the guidance. A chat channel holds the community, for help, sharing builds and celebrating them. Weekly drop-in hours give people someone to ask.</p>
        <p data-aud="pro">Each channel is the single home for one kind of support, so none of them has to do everything.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="3" id="s-sys-3"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Celebrate starts</p>
        <h3>“No success is too small”</h3>
        <p>I treat this as a design principle. It lowers the bar for a first build and makes early wins visible to everyone else.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="4" id="s-sys-4"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Before launch</p>
        <h3>Risks named early</h3>
        <p>I find it helps to name the risks before launch and give each one an owner. At Brindle Lake they might be branch shifts that clash with live sessions, part-time staff without access to the tool, and no agreed home for what people build<span class="gloss" data-aud="gen"> (a shared place where builds are stored and can be found)</span>.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="0,1">
          <span class="lab">The loop</span>
          <svg class="loop" viewBox="0 0 340 214" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="A loop: activate, learn, build, support, listen, adapt, and back to activate. What people said fed the next round."></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="2,3">
          <span class="lab">Each question goes to the channel built for it · illustrative questions</span>
          <div class="routes">
