            <span class="q">“Has anyone hit this error before?”</span><i>→</i><span class="ch"><b>Chat</b>community</span>
            <span class="q">“Can someone look at my flow with me?”</span><i>→</i><span class="ch"><b>Drop-in</b>a person</span>
            <span class="q tag" data-on="3">“I automated the holds list!”</span><i class="tag" data-on="3">→</i><span class="ch tag" data-on="3"><b>Chat</b>celebrated</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="4">
          <span class="lab">Risks named before launch · invented for the example</span>
          <div class="risk"><span class="x">risk</span><span>Shifts that clash with live sessions <span class="owned">owner named</span></span></div>
          <div class="risk"><span class="x">risk</span><span>Part-time staff without access <span class="owned">owner named</span></span></div>
          <div class="risk"><span class="x">risk</span><span>No agreed home for builds <span class="owned">owner named</span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HUMAN + AI -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="collaboration" aria-labelledby="h-col">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Human + AI</p>
    <h2 id="h-col">AI keeps the record and helps grade the story</h2>
    <p>In this approach, AI supports three parts: the record, the teaching and the look back.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-col-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Planning</p>
        <h3>Meeting notes became the working record</h3>
        <p>An AI note-taker captures the planning meetings. Once a person has checked them, those notes become the record for decisions, risks and follow-up tasks.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-col-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Teaching</p>
        <h3>AI alongside automation</h3>
        <p>I teach the AI assistant next to the automation tool, not as a separate course. It works as a self-paced aid people can ask while they build.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-col-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Looking back</p>
        <h3>A look back that grades itself</h3>
        <p>When I look back on a program, I use AI to rebuild its history from the sources. Interpretation stays separate from the source record, and anything I can't verify gets marked.</p>
        <p>This page does the same: <a href="#claims">every claim is graded at the end ↓</a></p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
