<section class="wrap outcome" id="outcome" aria-labelledby="oc-h">
  <p class="eyebrow">The approach · one way among several</p>
  <h2 id="oc-h" style="margin-top:8px">Three moves that have worked for me</h2>
  <div class="oc-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>Make the first example familiar</h3>
      <p>Use something people have already done, like signing up, so the explanation lands on experience instead of theory.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Name pages for goals</h3>
      <p>Label support by the goal a person arrives with, not by the categories its owners use.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Give each channel one job</h3>
      <p>Guidance, community and a person to ask each get one home, so none of them has to do everything.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="reflect">In my practice, people adopt technology faster when the environment is organized around what they're trying to do, <span>and when the first example is something they've already experienced.</span></p>
</section>

<section class="wrap claims" id="claims" aria-labelledby="h-claims">
  <p class="eyebrow">What it can claim</p>
  <h2 id="h-claims" style="margin-top:8px">What this story can support, and what it can't yet</h2>
  <p>I graded these myself. “Observed” means you can see it on this page. “Inferred” means my professional judgement, not tested here.</p>
  <details class="claimsbox"><summary>Claims register · 8 claims, and how well each is supported</summary>
  <dl class="legend">
    <div><dt><span class="cl">observed</span></dt><dd>Visible on this page, such as the sign-up simulation.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="cl doc">document-supported</span></dt><dd>Established by a linked public source.</dd></div>
