  </dl>
  <div class="regwrap">
    <table class="reg">
      <caption class="sr">Claims register</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">Claim</th><th scope="col">What supports it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr data-ref="s-show-1"><td><span class="cl">observed</span></td><td>A sign-up automation runs four steps: take the response, check the calendar, route to a session, send a confirmation.</td><td>The simulation on this page.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-show-2"><td><span class="cl">observed</span></td><td>When the schedule changes, the automation re-routes the registration.</td><td>The simulation, step three.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-show-3"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, using an automation before it's explained helps the explanation land faster.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-fd-3"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, support pages named for goals help people take the next step better than category folders do.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-sys-2"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, giving each channel one job keeps any one channel from having to do everything.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-sys-3"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, celebrating first builds lowers the bar for the next person.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="s-sys-4"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, naming risks and owners before launch is cheaper than finding them after.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
        <tr data-ref="outcome"><td><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></td><td>In my experience, people adopt technology faster when support is organized around their goals and the first example is one they've experienced.</td><td>My practice.</td></tr>
